   one thing in this panel that repaints its whole width on every frame, and blending made that repaint

   recomposite against the rail as well. The gradient's two light stops carry the ~12% more alpha the

   blend was contributing. What is left is a plain repaint of a static gradient, which is the cheapest

   form this sweep has short of rebuilding it as a translated layer. */

.cg-model-slider-shell[data-ultra="true"]::after {

